# Feature: Idea & concept management

Captures the starting point of every design: a unique Idea Reference, product
type, collection, season, style, concept note, plus images and files.

## Behavior
- Multi-image upload per design; exactly one image can be marked primary.
- Component-level breakdown (e.g. Pallu, Blouse, Sleeve, Front/Back) so images
  and specs attach to the correct part of the garment.
- Celebrity/trend reference fields and free-text concept notes.
- Product-type-aware validation via `ProductProcessMapping` (e.g. Saree
  requires Pallu/Blouse; Kurti requires Sleeve/Front/Back).

## Save sequence (must be one transaction)
1. Validate required concept fields and product type.
2. Create `DesignConcept` with a generated unique `IdeaRef`.
3. Save `DesignComponent` rows and `DesignImage` metadata.
4. Resolve selected Main Process / Sub-process.
5. Generate or accept `DesignTask` rows (see `12-feature-task-allocation.mdc`).
6. Write `AuditLog` entries and employee notifications.
7. Commit only if design, tasks, and mandatory metadata all succeed.

## Entities
`DesignConcept`, `DesignComponent`, `DesignImage`.

## API
- `POST /api/designs` - create concept + tasks in one transaction.
- `GET /api/designs`, `GET /api/designs/{id}` - search / full detail.
- `PATCH /api/designs/{id}` - allowed concept updates only.
- `POST /api/designs/{id}/images` - upload/register an image.

## User story seeds
- As a Design Head, I want to register a new idea with images and a concept
  note so the design can start moving through the pipeline.
